- Use edge labels such as `yes`, `no`, `retry`, or short branch names when helpful
- Decision branches should normally use labels on outgoing edges
- Keep the graph connected whenever possible

Validation rules:
- The model must start with one initial node
- The model must end with at least one final node
- Every edge must connect valid nodes
- Decision branches should reconnect using merge nodes when the topology plan expects closure
- Parallel branches should reconnect using join nodes when the topology plan expects closure
- Loops must include an exit path

